// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`help > root --help is stable 1`] = `
"Usage: vobiz [options] [command]

Vobiz CLI: voice calls, conferences, SMS/MMS/RCS, phone numbers, SIP trunks,
VobizXML and the Vobiz agent tools.

Options:
  -V, --version                  print the CLI version
  --profile <name>               saved login to use (env: VOBIZ_PROFILE)
  --auth-id <id>                 one-off Auth ID (env: VOBIZ_AUTH_ID)
  --auth-token <token>           one-off Auth Token; lands in shell history
                                 (env: VOBIZ_AUTH_TOKEN)
  -o, --output <format>          output format (env: VOBIZ_OUTPUT; default:
                                 table on a terminal, json when piped) (choices:
                                 "table", "json", "yaml", "tsv", "plain")
  --json                         shorthand for --output json
  --fields <paths>               comma-separated fields to show (dot paths, e.g.
                                 id,meta.total)
  -q, --quiet                    print only ids, one per line
  -y, --yes                      skip confirmation prompts; required for writes
                                 when stdin is not a terminal (env: VOBIZ_YES)
  --dry-run                      show the request (secrets redacted) and exit
                                 without sending
  --wait                         for calls and messages: wait until a final
                                 status
  --base-url <url>               voice API base URL (env: VOBIZ_BASE_URL)
  --sms-base-url <url>           Messaging API base URL (env:
                                 VOBIZ_SMS_BASE_URL)
  --timeout <seconds>            per-request timeout in seconds (env:
                                 VOBIZ_TIMEOUT; default: 30)
  --no-color                     disable colors (env: NO_COLOR)
  --verbose                      log requests (method, route, status, duration)
                                 to stderr
  --debug                        also log request and response bodies, secrets
                                 redacted (env: VOBIZ_LOG=debug)
  --no-update-check              skip the daily version check (env:
                                 VOBIZ_NO_UPDATE_CHECK, CI)
  -h, --help                     display help for command

Commands:
  login [options]                Save and verify a Vobiz Auth ID and Auth Token
                                 as a profile
  logout [options]               Remove saved credentials (the selected profile,
                                 or --all)
  whoami [options]               Show the account, Auth ID and credential source
                                 in use (offline; --check verifies with the API)
  profiles                       List, switch, rename and remove saved logins
  config                         Read and change CLI settings (output, color,
                                 updateCheck, telemetry, defaultProfile)
  doctor [options]               Check Node.js, config permissions,
                                 connectivity, credentials, clock skew and proxy
                                 settings
  update [options]               Check for a newer CLI version and show how to
                                 upgrade
  xml                            Build, validate and locally serve VobizXML
                                 call-control documents
  webhooks                       Verify Vobiz webhook signatures and receive
                                 webhooks locally
  mcp                            Connect Claude, Cursor, Codex, VS Code and
                                 other AI clients to the Vobiz MCP server
  skills                         Install the Vobiz Agent Skills into a project
                                 for Claude Code, Codex and other agents
  docs                           Search the Vobiz documentation and open pages
                                 in your browser
  api [options] [method] [path]  Send a raw request to the Vobiz API, or list
                                 and describe every operation in the spec
  completion <shell>             Print a shell completion script (bash, zsh,
                                 fish or powershell)
  help [words...]                Show help for a command, or a topic:
                                 exit-codes, env, output

Run \`vobiz help exit-codes\`, \`vobiz help env\` or \`vobiz help output\` for scripting details.
Docs: https://www.vobiz.ai/docs
"
`;
